# Algosize Worker — local development secrets.
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in. Wrangler loads this file
# automatically when you run `wrangler dev`. Do NOT commit `.dev.vars`.
#
# In production these values are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`
# instead — see comments in wrangler.toml.

# 32+ random bytes. Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=replace_with_long_random_string_at_least_32_bytes_please

# Stripe — use TEST keys locally.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_replace_me

# Tiered pricing — one price per (plan × interval), matching the three tiers
# on the pricing page. A tier with no price set here is REFUSED by
# POST /api/checkout with 503 plan_not_available; it never falls back to
# another price, so an unconfigured tier can't silently bill the wrong
# amount. Leave them unset until the prices exist in Stripe.
#
# The optional _SEAT companion is for a tier that charges a base fee plus a
# per-seat fee (Practice: $149 + $39/seat). Base is billed at quantity 1 and
# the seat price carries the seat count.
#
# STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_MONTHLY=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO_ANNUAL=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_MONTHLY=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_MONTHLY_SEAT=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_ANNUAL=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRACTICE_ANNUAL_SEAT=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_FIRM_MONTHLY=price_replace_me
# STRIPE_PRICE_FIRM_ANNUAL=price_replace_me

# Google Workspace — transactional email via Gmail API (Task #56).
# Leave UNSET locally to disable email sends; sendTransactional will
# no-op with a single warn-level log line. To exercise the real send
# path, paste the full JSON of a service-account key (one line, with
# embedded \n inside the private_key string preserved):
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"algosize-mailer@<proj>.iam.gserviceaccount.com",...}

# Google sign-in — OAuth 2.0 client (DEPLOY.md §3.7).
# A DIFFERENT credential from GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON above: that one is a
# service account for sending mail, this one is an OAuth client for signing
# users in. Leave both UNSET locally and the "Sign in with Google" button
# redirects to /?auth=google_not_configured — magic-link still works, so dev
# needs no Google setup at all.
#
# To exercise the real flow locally, register
#   http://localhost:8787/api/auth/google/callback
# as an additional authorised redirect URI on the same OAuth client. The URI
# must match ${SITE_ORIGIN}/api/auth/google/callback character for character,
# or Google fails with redirect_uri_mismatch before the Worker is reached.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-replace_me
